+  {
+    question: "Why does my cat bring me dead animals?",
+    answer:
+      "Your cat is doing you a favour — from their perspective. Cats are instinctive hunters, and presenting prey to you is a gesture of trust and affection. Some behaviourists also suggest cats may be trying to teach you hunting skills, just as a mother cat would teach her kittens. The best response is to calmly dispose of the gift and give your cat some praise.",
+  },
+  {
+    question: "Is it safe to let my cat go outside?",
+    answer:
+      "Outdoor cats enjoy more stimulation but face real risks: traffic, predators, disease, and parasites. Indoor cats typically live longer (12–18 years vs. 5–7 years on average). A good middle ground is a secure outdoor enclosure (\"catio\") or supervised leash walks. If your cat does go outdoors, ensure they're microchipped, vaccinated, and on a flea/tick prevention programme.",
+  },
+  {
+    question: "How can I stop my cat from scratching furniture?",
+    answer:
+      "Scratching is a natural need — cats scratch to stretch muscles, shed old nail sheaths, and mark territory. Instead of stopping the behaviour, redirect it:\n\nProvide sturdy scratching posts or boards (sisal fabric is a favourite).\nPlace them near the spots your cat currently scratches.\nUse double-sided tape on furniture as a temporary deterrent.\nTrim your cat's nails every 2–3 weeks.\nNever punish scratching — it won't work and damages trust.",
+  },
+  {
+    question: "Why does my cat meow so much?",
+    answer:
+      "Interestingly, adult cats almost never meow at other cats — they developed the behaviour specifically to communicate with humans. Common reasons include hunger, a request for attention, boredom, pain, or stress. If your cat's vocalisations increase suddenly or seem different in tone, it's worth a vet visit to rule out medical causes like hyperthyroidism or cognitive changes in older cats.",
+  },
+];
+
+function FaqItem({ question, answer, index }) {
+  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false);
+  const id = `faq-${index}`;
+
+  const formattedAnswer = answer.split("\n").map((line, i) => {
+    if (line.startsWith("- ") || line.startsWith("• ")) {
+      return line.slice(2);
+    }
+    return line;
+  });
+
+  const hasBullets = answer.includes("\n");
+
+  return React.createElement(
+    "div",
